Restore the original saved lap-record WORDs and 80-byte name-bank stride.

Update_Jimmy_Spunk_Times @44d868..44d871 computes saved index * 80.
The saved minute, second and fraction fields are unsigned WORDs, zero-extended
at 44d878/44d87f/44d890 and stored as WORDs at 44d972/44d983/44d99b.
Their BYTE aliases made param_1 * 0x28 advance 40 rather than 80 bytes and
truncated comparisons/stores. It prompted for equal/slower records, missed
faster records and damaged the saved times. Restore the unsigned WORD views.

The accepted-name destination @44d8e7..44d8ec is 4680c0 + index*80. Restore
the four-byte view used by the C expression &fastest_laps + index*0x14.
Its other typed DWORD copy loops and explicit byte addresses keep their
existing layout. Individual names remain char copies, and each track keeps
five consecutive 16-byte entries shifted in the original order.

The fixture executes the unchanged original comparison/history/time/name
machine code. A hardware breakpoint supplies only the name-entry callback's
0/1 return with an identical prepopulated name buffer on every target; no
original instructions are changed. It compares all targeted bytes/guards
and the prompt decisions. This controlled component check does not prove
the live name UI, actual saved cards, ordinary races or original A/V parity.

